#para([#text("The mouse can ordinarily stay on between uses, because it drops into a low-power idle state. You can still switch it off for transport or long storage. Its switch has no effect on the keyboard.")])
#subhead("USB devices and controllers")
#para([#text("Plug the USB hub into the rear USB-C port when you need more than one USB connection, or when a device has an older USB plug. The two game controllers are in the accessory pouch. Chapter 3 explains the game launcher. Use the cables or adapters that came with the controllers, and don’t force a plug into the hub.")])
#subhead("Bose speakers and stands")
#para([#text("The Bose speakers are an optional extra, not part of the PiForma package; they do not fit in the bag. The pair shown are 1984 Bose RoomMate speakers. They are almost as large as the PiForma’s screen, which makes for a great deal of sound from a very small picture, and they were chosen because their proportions match.")])
#para([#text("Connect the speakers to the rear audio output socket, then send the sound there with Sound Options, in the Wi-Fi status menu at the far right of the menu bar. Chapter 3 shows the menu. Give the speakers a stable place beside the working area, with cables out of the way and no strain on the PiForma. Their stands should not make the table or the computer’s folding stand unstable.")])
#wide-illustration("1-5", "complete-setup.png", "The complete setup: the PiForma on its stand, the keyboard in front, the mouse on its pad, a Bose speaker on its stand at each side and a game controller at the left.", width:263.115pt)
#subhead("Bringing sound into the PiForma")
#para([#text("The external audio adapter brings sound from another device, such as a VCR or a games console, into the PiForma over USB, so it plays through the PiForma’s speakers. That makes it external audio into the computer; sound going out uses the rear audio socket, as described above. The rear RCA jack carries only the picture.")])
#heading(level:2,"Important safety instructions")
#para([#text("Keep liquids away, protect the display, and leave ventilation openings clear. Keep the PiForma out of direct sun. Use a stable stand on a level table. Do not carry the computer by cables or press on the screen to move it.")])
#para([#text("The power switch does not disconnect external charging power from the internal charger. Switching it off doesn’t make the inside safe to work on. Never open it up with charging power connected, and leave internal repairs to us.")])
#para([#text("Stop using the computer if it becomes unusually hot, smells hot, or has damaged power wiring or a damaged battery. Don’t keep trying to switch it on. Charge it only with its own power cable or the bag’s charging cord. It was built at home, so it carries no safety certification.")])
#para([#text("Stop using it, too, if the screen starts to flicker. A flicker can have several causes, and it needs our attention before the next session.")])
#heading(level:2,"Starting up the computer")
#annotated("The startup chime",[#text("A silent startup doesn’t mean anything has failed, because some chime positions are silent. Go by the green light and the screen as well.")],[
