#screen-figure("1-8","piforma-about-system.svg","Apple menu → About This PiForma opens the information window.",width:300pt)
#para([#text("If the launcher or menu bar is missing, see Appendix B rather than trying unfamiliar touch gestures. When you have finished using the computer, follow “Stopping the computer” below.")])
#heading(level:2,"Power for a longer session")
#para([#text("If the internal battery is charged, you do not need a power cord for a short session. A full charge typically lasts about six hours of general use, or about four hours of emulated games, especially graphics-intensive ones. For longer sessions, keep the PiForma connected to external power when it is available.")])
#para([#text("The desktop has no battery gauge, and there is no low-battery warning. Check the battery display through the top slits now and then. When the battery runs out, the PiForma stops at once, just as if the power switch had been turned off, and unsaved work is lost. After a full drain, connect external power and allow a minute or two before it will start.")])
#para([#text("Take the power cable from the brown pouch. The original rear AC inlet supplies the internal charger. The battery can charge while the computer’s power switch is off. Use that cable rather than another charger.")])
#heading(level:2,"Stopping the computer")
#screen-figure("1-9","piforma-shutdown-menu.svg","Choose Shut Down from the Special menu after saving your work. This view shows the menu choice, not completed shutdown.",width:242pt)
#instruction(1,[#strong[#text("Save your work and leave any game or application using its own quit command when available.")] #text("If a full-screen program gives you no way out, hold the Apple logo for about six seconds instead.")])
#instruction(2,[#strong[#text("In the PiForma Panel menu bar, choose Special → Shut Down.")]])
#instruction(3,[#strong[#text("If a confirmation appears, choose Shut Down.")] #text("Let the operating system finish shutting down before removing physical power. A dark screen can also just mean the display is asleep, so give shutdown time to finish.")])
#instruction(4,[#strong[#text("Once shutdown is complete, turn off the power switch on the right side.")] #text("The green light at the front goes out. The wiring permits battery charging while the switch is off.")])
#para([#text("Never skip that last step. Shut Down stops the software but leaves the power on, and the battery drains quickly until the green light goes out. That matters most in the bag, where you can’t see the light.")])
#para([#text("Switching off without shutting down first is a last resort, for a computer that won’t respond. It can lose unsaved work or damage files.")])
#para([#text("To leave a full-screen program rather than stop the computer, see “Leaving a full-screen program” in Chapter 3. A hold of about six seconds closes only the active application on the current PiForma.")])
#heading(level:2,"Packing the equipment")
#instruction(1,[#strong[#text("Shut down properly, switch off physical power so the green light is out, and disconnect external cables as needed.")] #text("Make sure the computer and accessories are cool and dry before putting them away.")])
#instruction(2,[#strong[#text("Place the PiForma in the bag with its monitor/screen facing upward.")] #text("Its rear/bottom must seat in the molded indents in the bottom foam insert.")])
