#para([#text("The bag closes like an old canvas military bag. Feed the strap loop through the four grommets around the top, pass the clasp through the loop, and snap the clasp shut. To open the bag, do the same in reverse.")])
]
#wide-illustration("1-7b", "bag-clasp.png", "Pass the clasp through the strap loop and snap it shut.", width:137.655pt)
#subhead("Carrying the bag")
#para([#text("Carry the closed bag carefully. Its padding protects the PiForma during normal handling. Don’t drop it. We never crash tested this model, so don’t be the first to find out what happens. The Bose speakers travel separately, as described earlier in this chapter.")])
#heading(level:2,"If the PiForma doesn’t start")
#para([#text("Most startup trouble comes down to the battery, so begin there. Then find the symptom that matches what you see and hear. Appendix B repeats these checks in brief and covers problems after startup.")])
#subhead("Checking the battery")
#para([#text("If nothing happens, check the battery before assuming something has broken. The outside plunger mechanically presses the button on the internal battery pack, showing its charge indicators; pressing it may also wake or enable the pack.")])
#block(breakable:false,sticky:true)[
#para([#text("The normal, management-approved way to read the battery is to press the rear battery plunger to turn on its display, then peer through the slits in the top to see the percentage. You do not have to open the compartment for this check.")])
]
#wide-illustration("1-6a", "1-6b.png", "Read the battery percentage through the top slits after pressing the rear battery plunger. The eye shows where to look.", width:173.333pt)
#para([#text("Press the plunger, read the battery, and try the power switch again. If the battery is empty, seems asleep, or won’t start despite showing charge, plug in the power cable and try again.")])
#para([#text("If it still won’t start, connect the power cable and wait roughly a minute before trying again. We’ve had this work even when the battery previously showed full. Try it before taking anything apart, but do not count on one minute as a fixed recovery time. We don’t know why it works either.")])
#subhead("If there is no green light")
#para([#text("If there is no green light, no chime, and no picture, start with the power switch, battery indication, plunger and power cable. Then try again. If that doesn’t help, don’t go looking inside; ask us.")])
#subhead("If the light is on but there is no chime")
#para([#text("Some positions on the rear chime-selector dial are intentionally silent or empty. With the PiForma powered on, move the dial through several positions in either direction and listen for an available sound.")])
#para([#text("If it never sounds, the chime module may need attention, which is a job for us. The chime has its own sound hardware, so desktop sound can still work without it.")])
#subhead("If the light and chime work but the screen stays blank")
#para([#text("No Signal and a moment of blank screen are normal at first. If the startup picture has not appeared after about 15 seconds, press the source selector at the back until the screen shows HDMI. The chime plays before the computer has finished starting, so wait for the picture. If the picture stays blank, flickers or distorts, ask us rather than disturbing anything inside.")])
#subhead("If the desktop is slow to appear")
#para([#text("Give the computer one to two minutes to reach the desktop. If it stays on the startup picture, note what you see and tell us rather than switching it off and on repeatedly.")])
